<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mary of Guise</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1515">1515</a>–<a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Mary of Lorraine · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-guise">House of Guise</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mary of Guise was a daughter of Claude, first duke of Guise, of a cadet branch of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, and the wife of James V of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Mother of Mary, Queen of Scots, she governed Scotland as regent from 1554, keeping it allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Her rule was challenged by the Protestant Lords of the Congregation, and she died in 1560 during their rebellion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mary-of-guise.jpg" alt="Mary of Guise" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Corneille de Lyon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attributed_to_Corneille_de_Lyon_-_Mary_of_Guise,_1515_-_1560._Queen_of_James_V_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A younger son of René II founded the house of Guise in France, which led the Catholic League during the Wars of Religion and gave Scotland <b>Mary of Guise</b>, mother of Mary, Queen of Scots.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-lorraine">Duchy of Lorraine · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bar-le-duc">Bar-le-Duc</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in Edinburgh Castle, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=48.77,5.17&amp;year=1544" aria-label="Bar-le-Duc on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4670 460 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mary of Guise"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5120 730h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5120 730h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=48.77,5.17&amp;year=1544">What was here in 1544? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
